              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Lesions neither consistent nor pathognomonic hepatic/renal function. Hepatic damage may on necropsy (gross or histopathology). develop 48–72 hours later. Rhabdomyolysis-",
              "pdf_page": 984,
              "printed_page": 902,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Gastric contents may have a formaldehyde induced acute renal failure rare but possible. odor.",
